---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_URL, LEGAL_ENTITY } from '../lib/links';

export const prerender = true;

const updated = '2026-09-30';
---

<Base title="Terms" description="Terms of use for the scoop.md extension, library and website.">
  <article class="wrap page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">terms</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time></p>

    <p>
      These terms cover the scoop.md extension, the shared library at <code>api.scoop.md</code> and this website, run by{' '}
      <span class="placeholder">{LEGAL_ENTITY}</span>. By using them you agree to these terms. How we handle data is in
      the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Using scoop.md</h2>
    <p>You may use scoop.md for any lawful purpose. Don't:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>share material that isn't public documentation, or that you have no right to share;</li>
      <li>try to get instructions, malware or anything misleading into a scoop;</li>
      <li>cast votes or reports in bulk, rotate install IDs, or otherwise game the "worked" signal or rate limits;</li>
      <li>load the library or this website in ways that degrade them for others, or probe them for vulnerabilities without permission;</li>
      <li>use scoop.md to break a documentation site's own terms.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may block installs or addresses that do these things, and remove what they shared.</p>

    <h2>Content belongs to its publishers</h2>
    <p>
      Documentation in the library is copied from public pages and belongs to the people who published it. Every scoop
      keeps the URL of each source so the publisher is credited and the original is one click away. We don't claim
      ownership of it, and sharing a scoop doesn't give anyone rights to it beyond what its publisher allows.
    </p>
    <p>
      By sharing a scoop, voting or reporting, you let us store and display that contribution to run the library.
    </p>

    <h2>Takedowns</h2>
    <p>
      Use the report button in the extension, or email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the
      site and what's wrong. We review reports and remove scoops that are inaccurate, harmful or shared without the
      right to share them. Publishers can ask us to stop storing scoops for their site altogether.
    </p>

    <h2>The code</h2>
    <p>
      The extension's source is on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> under the license in that repository. Those license
      terms govern the code; these terms govern the hosted library and website.
    </p>

    <h2>What your agent does is up to you</h2>
    <p>
      A scoop is reference material. Your coding agent decides what to do with it, and you decide what to run, merge and
      ship. Review what it writes.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      scoop.md is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. Scoops can be incomplete, out of date or wrong, and
      the library may be unavailable. To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for losses arising from using
      scoop.md or anything it copies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The date above changes when we do; continuing to use scoop.md means you accept the
      update.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="placeholder">{LEGAL_ENTITY}</span>, <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 4vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
